 <section class="overview-hero about-hero">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">About Me · Durham, North Carolina</p><h1>I’m Daniel Winfield.</h1><div class="bio">
   <p>I’m pursuing an M.S. in Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science at Duke University after earning my B.S. in Mechanical Engineering from Tuskegee University. My work brings together mechanical design, robotics, embedded systems, computer vision, and experimental testing.</p>
   <p>I’m most engaged when I can work directly with a physical system: developing CAD, fitting parts together, integrating sensors and electronics, and testing how a prototype behaves. I enjoy the iteration between a design on screen and what happens at the workbench.</p>
   <p>Through individual builds, team projects, and research, I’ve worked on robotic manipulation, interactive Raspberry Pi systems, image-based measurement, and materials characterization. I’m interested in robotics, mechatronics, and product development roles that combine mechanical design with hands-on hardware work.</p>
